---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import site from '@data/site.json';

---

<BaseLayout
  title={`About ${site.name}`}
  description={`What ${site.name} is, who makes it and how the ideas are put together.`}
  path="/about/"
  crumbs={[
    { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
    { label: 'About us', href: '/about/' },
  ]}
>
  <section class="container page-top">
    <h1>About us</h1>
    <div class="lead">
      <p>{site.name} is a reference library for people planning a tattoo.</p>
      <p>Browse by placement, size, style and subject, then walk into the studio knowing what to ask.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section container prose">
    <h2>Why this site exists</h2>
    <p>
      Most tattoo inspiration lives on social platforms, where you cannot filter
      by body area or size, and where the same image gets reposted without any
      idea of how big it actually is. Every image here carries the placement,
      the size in centimetres, the style and the colour as text you can read.
    </p>

    <h2>What we do differently</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Filters that are real pages, so a combination you want has a link you can send someone.</li>
      <li>A shortlist you can build without an account and take to your appointment.</li>
      <li>A brief you can copy and hand to your artist in plain words.</li>
      <li>Size compared on a real body, not as a circle on a white page.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Who makes it</h2>
    <p>
      TattooDesignsCo is maintained as an independent editorial reference
      project. Pages are organised from search research, then reviewed for a
      clear relationship between the image, placement label, size and style.
      Commercial relationships do not determine which idea appears first.
    </p>
    <p>
      We are not a tattoo studio and do not accept bookings. The purpose of the
      site is to help you prepare a more precise conversation with an artist who
      can adapt a concept to your body and draw an original version.
    </p>

    <h2>Images and artists</h2>
    <p>
      How images are sourced and checked is written out in full on the
      <a href="/editorial-standards/">editorial standards</a> page. If you are an
      artist and want your work featured with a credit, or you have found your
      work here without permission, write to
      <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>What this site is not</h2>
    <p>
      It is not medical guidance. Anything about healing, skin reactions,
      allergies or removal is a question for your artist or a doctor, and we
      will always say so rather than answer it ourselves.
    </p>

    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      If a caption names the wrong placement, size, style or colour, send the
      page address and identify the image. We review factual corrections and
      rights requests before general partnership messages. The contact page
      explains what information helps us investigate quickly.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
